ore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a82f03-efa1-504e-80f8-4b017713e4f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378190} {:answer/id #uuid "0baa6114-af76-53b7-a9c7-022cb452550a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378191} {:answer/id #uuid "e35de28a-6dfc-58db-b2ab-af8b18b12b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378192} {:answer/id #uuid "210f1082-3a14-5e89-8d10-ed7a2c6b1d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378193} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6eb4c1-c4b0-5fdf-9d80-e216c1f6fde6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e35de28a-6dfc-58db-b2ab-af8b18b12b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378192} :answer-field/id #uuid "c332d7e7-5c3e-5d52-9494-b6aeb2c207b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "897313ab-8a44-5c6f-bd61-a0fa12f9c240" :question/math-academy-id "q-103062" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $G?$\n\n- $(H∨G)∧G$\n- $H∧(H∨G)$\n- $(G∨H)∨G$" :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nG∧(G∨H)≡G.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(H∨G)∧G & ≡G∧(H∨G) \\\\  & ≡G∧(G∨H) \\\\  & ≡G.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H∧(H∨G) & ≡H≢G.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $G.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8bc9176-817d-55a3-b3fa-f704413af082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378197} {:answer/id #uuid "d9adbd11-9e77-5157-b694-27b2f25e93be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378198} {:answer/id #uuid "a3010ec6-7cf7-5890-98d7-91dcac146296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378199} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ef0211-8b0a-5071-8ea5-9a6cce73c6ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378200} {:answer/id #uuid "692e20f0-bb5f-5c4a-a847-26cd93864aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9adbd11-9e77-5157-b694-27b2f25e93be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378198} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a378547-3a39-5ee5-855d-0bb581ff7675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4d683c7-8d10-55e5-a90e-d913d4664ae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103067" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $A?$\n\n- $¬B∧(A∨¬B)$\n- $(¬B∨A)∧A$\n- $A∧(¬B∨A)$" :question/worked-solution "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nA∧(A∨¬B)≡A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬B∧(A∨¬B) & ≡¬B∧(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡¬B≢A.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬B∨A)∧A & ≡A∧(¬B∨A) \\\\  & ≡A∧(A∨¬B) \\\\  & ≡A.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧(¬B∨A) & ≡A∧(A∨¬B) \\\\  & ≡A.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba3b1751-5953-5fca-8888-36a7a3297a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378204} {:answer/id #uuid "f02ab0f2-8c8d-5fd8-963f-d04a3c8c656b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III onl