uestion/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nM∨(M∧L)≡M.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(L∧M)∨M & ≡M∨(L∧M) \\\\  & ≡M∨(M∧L) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $M.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M∨(L∧M) & ≡M∨(M∧L) \\\\  & ≡M.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4ea352-2a82-5ff5-8c08-b7f9a09929e6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Disjunction Absorbs Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be3f373f-097e-5973-b701-d5b004c0fd53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378218} {:answer/id #uuid "70dc7167-be75-5b59-9080-653b2e08d444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378219} {:answer/id #uuid "112df888-f091-5999-b6e7-093fb47c02cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378220} {:answer/id #uuid "3e50ea63-ccfd-5b82-a88f-3ec1d14257b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378221} {:answer/id #uuid "ab633a40-ba15-55a8-8e21-728caf9da3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e50ea63-ccfd-5b82-a88f-3ec1d14257b6" :answer/type {:db/i